**what_frustrates_them:** Existing content picks ONE lever (just color, or just shape, or just gel-vs-acrylic) and leaves the other two unaddressed, forcing them to read 3 separate articles to make one decision.

**top_5_pain_points:**
1. Bold/opaque colors show a hard regrowth line within days — confirmed across hola.com, Women.com, Scratch Magazine.
2. Sharp-edged shapes (coffin, stiletto, sharp square) snag, chip, and look "grown out" faster than soft shapes — confirmed GelBottle, OPI, Maniology.
3. Not knowing the real fill/redo cadence difference between gel, acrylic, and regular polish before booking — confirmed L'Oréal, Glitterbels, thelocalgem.com.
4. Not knowing how to phrase the request to a nail tech without a trend name — confirmed via soap nails audience research (WhoWhatWear: "you don't need to know the trend name, just describe it").
5. Underlying cost/time frustration with frequent redos — confirmed Refinery29 "nail privilege" and TikTok "high maintenance to be low maintenance" trend (493M+ views cited).

**exact_user_phrases:** "grows out gracefully," "salon-fresh," "doesn't show regrowth immediately," "hide the gap near the cuticle," "just-washed look," "I woke up like this," "low-maintenance is for rookies" (ironic Pinterest usage — worth avoiding as unironic phrasing), "clients going a bit longer between appointments," "quiet luxury," "your-nails-but-better."

